<title>FRANCE: AT&amp;T, Alcatel to provide pan-American cable.</title>
<headline>AT&amp;T, Alcatel to provide pan-American cable.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>France's Alcatel Alsthom and U.S. AT&amp;T Corp said on Monday they would provide, for more than one billion francs, the first pan-American fibre-optic cable system to link the Caribbean, Central and South America.  </p>
<p>It said the new system would be owned by 13 of the world's leading telecommunications carriers, span more than 7,000 km and was expected to go into service on June 30, 1998.</p>
<p>Alcatel Submarine Networks and AT&amp;T Submarine Systems will be the major suppliers, an Alcatel statement said.</p>
<p>Major subcontractors will provide a variety of high-end optical equipment, fibre and cable for the system, it added.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
